# Machine-local overrides for check-public.sh
# This file is .gitignored and never published.
# Rename or copy this to `check-public.local` and edit to add patterns specific
# to your machine.
#
# Format: pattern|reason (one per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored)
#
# Examples:
#   myhost|my personal hostname
#   prod-server|production server domain
#   myrealname|names that should not leak into the tree
#   myproject|project name or infrastructure label
#
# The shipped check-public.sh provides:
#   - Generic patterns: private IP ranges, credential shapes (sk-, ghp_, AWS keys, etc.)
#   - Dynamic hostname check: whatever hostname -s and hostname -f return on this machine
#   - Real-looking /home/<user> paths (not /home/user or /home/user2 placeholders)
#
# Add machine-specific hostnames, usernames, project names, and infrastructure
# identifiers here to protect them from accidentally being committed to the
# published repository.
